//@version=6
// LIVE TEST LEVEL 2 — one real 1-contract FILL, then flatten on sight. SUPERVISED ONLY.
//
// @sandbox-expect: entry.placed entry.filled position>=1 close.placed close.filled
//   (sandbox grades the ORDER PATH only — not SL/TP/netting/P&L; position oscillates.)
//
// Gate: run ONLY after LEVEL 1 (live1/live2/live3 place+cancel) all pass. This is the FIRST
// test that takes a REAL position. It enters exactly ONE market long (1 contract) on the
// first realtime bar, then closes THAT entry on the NEXT evaluation after the position
// appears — so the contract is held ~1 bar. An enter-once latch makes it trade once and
// never again.
//
// Why each guard matters (verified against the runtime + plugin, not assumed):
//   * default_qty_value=1, pyramiding=0  -> one lot, never stacks.
//   * `var traded` enter-once latch       -> exactly one real entry for the whole run.
//   * `barstate.isrealtime` gate          -> the entry NEVER fires on historical warmup
//       (isrealtime is False in backtest/warmup, set True only on the live bar by the
//       engine). A plain `dnse:` backtest of this file therefore places ZERO orders —
//       that quiet backtest IS the safety proof that warmup cannot trade.
//   * price-less entry                    -> the plugin sends a MARKETABLE LO at the band
//       edge: it fills at market but cannot fill worse than the +/-7% band (capped slippage).
//   * strategy.close("E") (NOT close_all) -> flattens only OUR entry; an external/adopted
//       position is never touched (plugin reduce_only is software-enforced).
//
// PRECONDITION (hard): continuous session, FLAT account (no position, no working orders),
// operator watching, DNSE app open for one-tap manual flatten. See LIVE_TEST_PLAN_L2.md.
strategy("LIVE2 fill+flatten", overlay=true, pyramiding=0, initial_capital=500000000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1,
     margin_long=18.48, margin_short=18.48,
     slippage=1,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=false)

var bool traded  = false   // enter-once latch — one real entry for the whole run
var bool closing = false   // close-once latch — one flatten order

// (1) The single real entry — ONLY on the live bar, never during historical warmup.
if barstate.isrealtime and not traded
    strategy.entry("E", strategy.long, comment="MKT 1-lot")
    traded := true

// (2) Flatten OUR entry on the NEXT evaluation after a position appears.
//
// NOT "instantly", despite what this comment used to claim: order commit is DEFERRED, so
// `strategy.position_size` still reads 0 on the bar that places the entry. This block can
// therefore only become true one evaluation later (measured 2026-09-11: entry issued bar 1,
// position first visible bar 2). With calc_on_every_tick=false that is a full bar — at the
// 5m/15m timeframes this suite runs at, 5-15 minutes of REAL exposure, not an instant.
//
// ORDER MATTERS — cancel_all() MUST come BEFORE close(). Both execute in the same
// evaluation, and `strategy.cancel_all()` clears the exit-order book wholesale
// (BrokerPosition._cancel_all_orders -> exit_orders.clear()). A close() issued FIRST is
// stored in exactly that book and is wiped before OrderSyncEngine.sync() can dispatch it,
// so the flatten silently never reaches the venue. Measured 2026-09-11: as originally
// written the position stayed open indefinitely; both removing cancel_all and swapping
// these two lines flatten correctly. Block (3) below already used the correct order.
if traded and strategy.position_size != 0 and not closing
    strategy.cancel_all()   // explicit: the engine's implicit bracket
                            // teardown left an order working (see log 14:06)
    strategy.close("E", comment="FLATTEN")
    closing := true

// (3) DOUBLE-CHECK backstop at -0.3%: cancel every working order FIRST (so no resting
//     leg can re-open exposure right after the flatten), then flatten everything. With
//     flatten-on-sight above this should never fire — it exists for when that fails.
DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT = -0.3

// PnL% IS COMPUTED MANUALLY BELOW, ON PURPOSE. `strategy.opentrades.profit_percent()`
// returns 0.0 for an OPEN trade in PyneCore (and upstream): the per-bar update loop
// writes `trade.profit` only, and every `profit_percent` assignment lives in a CLOSE
// path. Measured 2026-09-11 — profit went 0 -> -2 -> -4 -> -6 while profit_percent
// stayed 0.0000 throughout. Using it made this whole backstop DEAD CODE: `0 < -0.3`
// is never true. Same defect the strategy repo documented in 2026-08.
// These ARE live on an open trade (measured in the same run): entry_price, size, profit.
// So the percentage is derived from price directly. `_bsDir` inverts it for a short —
// without it a losing short would report a gain.
// NOTE: this is pure PRICE movement, unlike the engine's profit_percent, which nets
// commission and divides by total entry cost. For an adverse-move safety stop that is
// the more appropriate measure, not merely an approximation of it.
_bsEntry = strategy.opentrades > 0 ? strategy.opentrades.entry_price(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0
_bsSize  = strategy.opentrades > 0 ? strategy.opentrades.size(strategy.opentrades - 1) : 0.0
_bsDir   = _bsSize < 0 ? -1.0 : 1.0
_bsLive = strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(_bsEntry) and _bsEntry != 0.0
openPnlPct = _bsLive ? (close - _bsEntry) / _bsEntry * 100.0 * _bsDir : 0.0
if strategy.position_size != 0 and openPnlPct < DOUBLE_CHECK_PCT
    strategy.cancel_all()
    strategy.close_all(comment="DOUBLECHECK")

plot(strategy.position_size, "pos", display=display.data_window)
